# Shell scripts must be LF — bash on Mac/Linux chokes on CRLF, even when
# invoked as `bash script.sh`. Same for any other Unix-side executable text.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Keep Python files LF for cross-platform consistency.
*.py   text eol=lf

# .mjs CLI scripts (scripts/*.mjs) open with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang.
# Vite/vitest's own shebang-stripping (used when a test imports one of these
# scripts) matches only an LF-terminated shebang line; on a CRLF checkout
# (windows-latest CI runners, or any Windows box without this rule) the match
# fails, the raw `#!...` line survives into the transformed module, and
# import blows up as "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" with no file
# or line — plain `node` and esbuild's own CLI both tolerate CRLF here fine,
# so this was invisible outside Vite's transform. Hit release-gate.test.ts,
# source-hygiene-gate.test.ts and gate-outcome-fires.contract.test.ts, all of
# which import a shebang'd script under scripts/.
*.mjs  text eol=lf

# Generated artifacts that a build gate byte-compares against freshly
# generated content must keep the generator's line endings in the working
# tree. gen-codebase-map.mjs emits LF and --check compares raw strings, so
# without this autocrlf hands Windows a CRLF checkout and `npm run build`
# fails "stale" on a map that is perfectly current.
docs/codebase-map.md text eol=lf
# Same reason, plus it keeps `git status` from reporting a permanent
# line-ending modification on a doc whose content is actually current.
docs/agent-capabilities.md text eol=lf
